From 672ada5cad5bf21740950f3bba42cb27d945bae5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:27:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(joint): fold both circuits' sumcheck tables in one
 largest-first parallel region

The joint sumcheck partially evaluated the MegaZK and translator tables with two
back-to-back parallel_for regions (46 + 190 polynomials of very different sizes),
each paying its own dispatch and load-imbalance tail. Fold both circuits' tables
from a single work list sorted largest-first. Same fold_stride2 per polynomial,
so every partial evaluation (and hence the proof) is unchanged.
